{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["The reason for <b>and when a sojourner sojourns with you</b> — to command the converts concerning this Passover of the wilderness, just as He commands it for Israel. And it is possible that what He said in the section 'Come to Pharaoh' — 'and when a sojourner sojourns with you and makes a Passover' (Exodus 12:48) — refers to the Passover of Egypt, for that passage was spoken about the Passover of Egypt, as I explained there, and it was understood to mean that the converts who came out of Egypt, the mixed multitude, would make a Passover, since they too were part of that miracle. But those who convert afterward in the wilderness or in the land of Israel would not be obligated in Passover, for neither they nor their fathers were included in 'us He brought out from there' (Deuteronomy 6:23). Therefore it was necessary here to obligate them in the Passover of the generations, in the wilderness and in the land."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:03:48.204778808Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}